WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:01.410
- How about this,

00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:04.450
because next up, clams
might be an aphrodisiac.

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:05.283
- [Ross] Yeah.

00:00:05.283 --> 00:00:08.960
- But apparently New York
City doesn't need one.

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:10.910
According to The Guardian,

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:15.117
noise complaints about
bedroom activity are way up.

00:00:15.117 --> 00:00:15.950
- [Ross] Wow.

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:17.349
- From burrow to burrow.

00:00:17.349 --> 00:00:18.267
(audience claps and cheers)

00:00:18.267 --> 00:00:20.310
People are getting busy,

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:22.820
and being real loud about it.

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:27.650
Last year, there were 277 noise
complaints relating to sex.

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:29.600
Queens had the most, at 103.

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:30.677
Good for you, Queens.

00:00:30.677 --> 00:00:31.510
(audience laughs)

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:32.343
- Yeah, Queens.

00:00:32.343 --> 00:00:34.710
- Manhattan had 66, Brooklyn, 55,

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:37.637
the Bronx 48, and Staten Island had four.

00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:41.240
(Ross and audience laugh)

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:43.670
Maybe we need to send
Staten Island some clams.

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:44.742
- [Ross] Hey.

00:00:44.742 --> 00:00:45.575
(Ross laughs)

00:00:45.575 --> 00:00:48.930
- So there were some
specificities in the complaints.

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:50.787
I'm quoting them right now,

00:00:50.787 --> 00:00:54.207
"She makes the bed squeak as
if it's an Olympic event".

00:00:54.207 --> 00:00:55.040
(audience laughs)

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:55.873
- [Ross] Wow.

00:00:55.873 --> 00:00:57.500
- [Drew, In A Deep Voice]
"I've slept through Earthquakes

00:00:57.500 --> 00:00:59.982
and fires, and I couldn't
sleep through this".

00:00:59.982 --> 00:01:01.070
- [Ross] Uh huh.

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:01.950
- I love this.

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:02.783
- I love this, too.

00:01:02.783 --> 00:01:03.616
Let me tell you,

00:01:03.616 --> 00:01:05.210
so we have been through
a rough couple years.

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:07.006
Go and get it, get yours, go for it.

00:01:07.006 --> 00:01:07.964
(Drew laughs)

00:01:07.964 --> 00:01:08.800
(audience claps)

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:10.605
And if you, I'm sorry,

00:01:10.605 --> 00:01:13.690
(audience claps)

00:01:13.690 --> 00:01:14.680
If I heard this,

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:17.027
I would not complain, as
long as it's not too loud.

00:01:17.027 --> 00:01:19.000
Just like, normal people,

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:20.887
two and a half, three minutes,
have fun doing a thing.

00:01:20.887 --> 00:01:22.960
(Drew laughs)

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:25.192
Have you ever like heard people, you know,

00:01:25.192 --> 00:01:26.258
having their kind of fun?

00:01:26.258 --> 00:01:27.091
- Not enough.

00:01:27.091 --> 00:01:27.924
- Not enough.

00:01:27.924 --> 00:01:29.550
- No, I would celebrate it.

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:30.383
- [Ross] Sure. I would, too.

00:01:30.383 --> 00:01:32.060
- And then I'd become
that old lady, you know?

00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:34.153
Who's like, I don't know,

00:01:34.153 --> 00:01:37.920
listen, knock the boots, do
the thing, have some fun.

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:38.753
- Do the thing, and if you-

00:01:38.753 --> 00:01:40.820
- Do you know how many of
my friends are pregnant

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:42.330
because of the pandemic?

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:43.163
- [Ross] Oh yeah.

00:01:43.163 --> 00:01:44.870
- I mean, it's such a baby boom.

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:45.703
- It is.

00:01:45.703 --> 00:01:47.180
- It's exciting.

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:50.760
Every single one of my
girlfriends is pregnant.

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:51.593
- Really?

00:01:51.593 --> 00:01:53.150
- Oh my God, everyone I know.

00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:53.983
- [Ross] Wow.

00:01:53.983 --> 00:01:54.816
- Pregnant.

00:01:54.816 --> 00:01:59.150
- Well, I've never like
heard people doing it, ever,

00:01:59.150 --> 00:02:00.160
but I want to so bad.

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:00.993
- [Drew] For real?

00:02:00.993 --> 00:02:01.826
- Yeah.

00:02:01.826 --> 00:02:02.730
And if I did, I would not complain.

00:02:02.730 --> 00:02:03.640
I would call all my best friend,

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:04.473
put it on speaker,

00:02:04.473 --> 00:02:05.629
and be like, "Listen", right?

00:02:05.629 --> 00:02:06.462
- [Drew] Totally.

00:02:06.462 --> 00:02:07.295
- Totally.

00:02:07.295 --> 00:02:08.128
- [Drew] I know.

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:08.961
- Get a life, don't complain.

00:02:08.961 --> 00:02:10.620
- I'm sure at like three in the morning,

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:11.453
I'd probably be like,

00:02:11.453 --> 00:02:13.260
"All right, you know, I gotta work".

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:15.360
But like, I don't think I would,

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:16.739
I would be happy for people.

00:02:16.739 --> 00:02:18.360
I'd say do it up.

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:20.860
- Yeah. Especially speaking
to you in Staten Island,

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:21.713
come on.

00:02:21.713 --> 00:02:22.546
(audience claps)

00:02:22.546 --> 00:02:23.379
- [Drew] Let's do this.

00:02:23.379 --> 00:02:24.212
- Step it up.

00:02:24.212 --> 00:02:25.849
All right, finally, oh, some noodle news.

00:02:25.849 --> 00:02:26.700
(Drew shrieks)

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:28.951
- That's my favorite kinda news, Rossy.

00:02:28.951 --> 00:02:29.784
(Drew slurps)

00:02:29.784 --> 00:02:31.261
- Yes, because we are
wrapping up our pasta week.

00:02:31.261 --> 00:02:33.090
- [Drew] Don't say it's going away.

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:34.600
- [Ross] Your favorite week of all, right?

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:35.433
- It is.

00:02:35.433 --> 00:02:37.630
I love a pasta, it's my
favorite food on planet Earth.

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:38.463
- It is.

00:02:38.463 --> 00:02:41.000
Well, PureWow reports
TikTok's found a new way

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:42.580
to strain your pasta.

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:44.980
Yeah, turns out you've been
doing it wrong all along.

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:46.890
Millions have viewed this hack.

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:50.850
They say, you should put
your strainer into the pot,

00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:55.850
then walk to the sink and
carefully pour out the water.

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:59.640
Because look, yeah, the
pasta never leaves the pot.

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:00.473
You understand?

00:03:00.473 --> 00:03:01.310
'Cause all the other time

00:03:01.310 --> 00:03:04.050
I've been like trying to hold strainer

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:06.410
and lift the thing, giving
myself that facial, you know,

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:09.550
and then lifting it out, and
I always lose a noodle or two.

00:03:09.550 --> 00:03:10.513
What do you think?

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:14.670
- I feel like this one
is a "Oh, duh" moment,

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:15.570
like in a good way.

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:16.430
Like, "Oh yeah".

00:03:16.430 --> 00:03:17.420
The only thing I would say is,

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:19.620
don't forget to get
the mug of pasta water,

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:21.170
'cause it's the magic ingredient.

00:03:21.170 --> 00:03:22.003
- [Ross] Oh, yes.

00:03:22.003 --> 00:03:22.836
- Which, by the way,

00:03:22.836 --> 00:03:24.944
sometimes on that walk,
is when I remember.

00:03:24.944 --> 00:03:26.660
(audience claps)

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:28.910
So like get it while it's good,

00:03:28.910 --> 00:03:30.650
because you'll dump that out,

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:33.060
and then all of a sudden you'll lose that.

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:34.250
You can't get anything.

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:36.180
There's nothing you can buy,

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:38.140
that compares with pasta water.

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:41.260
So save it, but I'm gonna try this.

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:42.710
- Yeah, just always save, you're right.

00:03:42.710 --> 00:03:43.790
Just a little bit of that starchy water,

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:45.450
'cause it will change your sauce game.

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:46.300
- It's the best thing,

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:50.143
it's the best thing you can
have in the pasta world.

00:03:50.143 --> 00:03:52.643
(light music)

